// Records the README demo animations from the real app.
//
//   node scripts/record-demo.mjs [frames-root]
//
// Prerequisites:
//   - `npm --prefix desktop/ui run ux:build` built the isolated UX app;
//   - msedgedriver is cached by `make ux-setup`;
//   - tauri-driver is installed;
//   - ffmpeg and gifsicle are on PATH (or set FFMPEG to ffmpeg's full path);
//   - `GENTREE_CHAT_API_KEY` is exported for the assistant part;
//   - the demo projects were generated by `node scripts/make-demo-project.mjs`.
//
// The script starts on an empty isolated library, imports a GEDCOM generated
// from the demo project through the real Import screen, and then drives the
// real UI over WebDriver. Every frame is a WebDriver screenshot of the window
// content, so no OS cursor, taskbar or other window can leak into the clip. The
// frames become docs/assets/demo.gif (light) and demo-ru.gif (Russian), their
// dark twins, and a demo.mp4 next to the run artifacts.
//
// The chat part uses the configured provider from the installed app's config;
// only the synthetic demo project is sent, and no key is ever printed or shown.
//
// It never reads a real archive and never opens the Settings screen.
//
// It never reads a real archive and never opens the Settings screen.

